# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 044 — supersedes gap-011
# Act: SEG*  (Segment aimed at Pattern)   Stance: Unraveling   Site: Network
#
# gap-011 refused this act for lack of a second field to generalize turn-
# 10's boundary against. That gap is superseded: turn-43 is a second,
# genuinely independent field (different kind, two-of-three members
# different, only the legitimately-shared control in common).
#
# The generalization checked, precisely: BOTH fields partition as
# "two independently-anchored kind-members on one side, the shared
# negative control alone on the other, with the kind's sign on one side
# and the control's sign on the other" —
#
#   turn-10:  {signal-a, signal-b | noise-control}   absent | present
#   turn-43:  {signal-c, signal-d | noise-control}   anomalous | ordinary
#
# — despite the two kinds sharing no mechanism (turn-10's sign comes from
# NUL's null-check; turn-43's from turn-31's magnitude-ground computation)
# and no members except the control. This is a stronger claim than any
# earlier Pattern-grain act in this kernel made: not "the same kind recurs"
# but "the same SHAPE of boundary recurs across two kinds that have
# nothing else in common." That is what NETWORK-level (SEG's Pattern-grain
# site) is supposed to mean, and this is the first turn in this kernel
# actually built at that grain rather than at Kind-grain.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-10 and turn-43, two independently
# earned partitions. Refuted if the two boundaries' shapes disagreed — one
# had three kind-members, say, or the control landed on the kind's side in
# either — checked directly above: both are exactly a 2-vs-1 split with the
# control isolated. They do not disagree.

:turn-44  eot:opens        :turn-43 .
:turn-44  eot:supersedes   :gap-011 .
:turn-44  eot:act          eot:SEG* .
:turn-44  eot:stance       "Unraveling" .
:turn-44  eot:site         "Network" .
:turn-44  eot:generalizes  :turn-10 .
:turn-44  eot:generalizes  :turn-43 .
:turn-44  eot:consistent   true .
:turn-44  eot:witnessed    true .
:turn-44  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
